00:50:17,281 --> 00:50:21,266
under the headboard, and the extra blanket folded neatly at the foot of the rack.

656
00:50:22,168 --> 00:50:29,668
It was a simple task. mundane at best, but every morning we were required to make our bed to perfection.

657
00:50:30,468 --> 00:50:37,668
It seemed a little ridiculous at the time, particularly in light of the fact that we were aspiring to be real warriors, tough, battle-hardened SEALs.

658
00:50:38,668 --> 00:50:43,668
But the wisdom of this simple act has been proven to me many times over.

659
00:50:44,868 --> 00:50:49,468
If you make your bed every morning, you will have accomplished the first task of the day.

660
00:50:50,368 --> 00:50:56,968
It will give you a small sense of pride, and it will encourage you to do another task, and another, and another.

661
00:50:57,668 --> 00:51:01,868
And by the end of the day, that one task completed will have turned into many tasks completed.

662
00:51:02,568 --> 00:51:06,968
Making your bed will also reinforce the fact But the little things in life matter.

663
00:51:07,768 --> 00:51:12,068
If you can't do the little things right, you'll never be able to do the big things right.

664
00:51:12,968 --> 00:51:17,368
And if by chance you have a miserable day, you will come home to a bed that is made.

665
00:51:19,468 --> 00:51:20,168
That you made.

666
00:51:21,468 --> 00:51:24,568
And a made bed gives you encouragement that tomorrow will be better.

667
00:51:25,468 --> 00:51:28,868
So if you want to change the world, start off by making your bed.

668
00:51:31,460 --> 00:51:36,960
During SEAL training, the students are all broken down into boat crews.

669
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:43,156
Each crew is seven students, three on each side of a small rubber boat, and one coxswain to help guide the dinghy.

670
00:51:44,260 --> 00:51:50,256
Every day, your boat crew forms up on the beach and is instructed to get through the surf zone and paddle several miles down the coast.

671
00:51:50,760 --> 00:51:54,435
In the winter, the surf off San Diego can get to be

672
00:51:54,435 --> 00:51:56,272
8 to 10 feet high, and it is

673
00:51:56,272 --> 00:51:59,947
exceedingly difficult to paddle through the plunging surf unless everyone digs in.

674
00:52:01,760 --> 00:52:05,660
Every paddle must be synchronized to the stroke count of the coxswain.

675
00:52:06,460 --> 00:52:13,057
Everyone must exert equal effort or the boat will turn against the wave and be unceremoniously dumped back on the beach.

676
00:52:14,060 --> 00:52:17,760
For the boat to make it to its destination, everyone must paddle.

677
00:52:18,960 --> 00:52:20,360
You can't change the world alone.

678
00:52:21,260 --> 00:52:22,160
You will need some help.

679
00:52:22,860 --> 00:52:26,940
And to truly get from your starting point to your destination takes

680
00:52:26,940 --> 00:52:31,360
friends, colleagues, the goodwill of strangers, and a strong coxswain to guide you.

681
00:52:32,060 --> 00:52:35,160
If you want to change the world, find someone to help you paddle.

682
00:52:37,332 --> 00:52:44,032
Over a few weeks of difficult training, my SEAL class, which started with 150 men, was down to just 42.

683
00:52:44,832 --> 00:52:46,932
There were now six boat crews of seven men each.

684
00:52:48,032 --> 00:52:55,729
I was in the boat with the tall guys, but the best boat crew we had was made up of the little guys, the munchkin crew we called them.

685
00:52:56,532 --> 00:52:58,032
No one was over 5'5".

686
00:52:59,332 --> 00:53:05,464
The Munchkin boat crew had one American Indian, one African American, one Polish American, one Greek American, one

687
00:53:05,464 --> 00:53:08,530
Italian American, and two tough kids from the Midwest.

688
00:53:09,332 --> 00:53:13,932
They out-paddled, out-ran, and out-swam all the other boat crews.

689
00:53:14,332 --> 00:53:18,632
The big men in the other boat crews would always make good-natured fun.

690
00:53:19,332 --> 00:53:25,832
Of the tiny little flippers the munchkins put on their tiny little feet prior to every swim.

691
00:53:27,132 --> 00:53:30,404
But somehow these little guys from every corner of the nation and

692
00:53:30,404 --> 00:53:32,585
the world always had the last laugh, swimming

693
00:53:32,585 --> 00:53:36,130
faster than everyone and reaching the shore long before the rest of us.

694
00:53:37,532 --> 00:53:39,032
SEAL training was a great equalizer.

695
00:53:39,832 --> 00:53:46,327
Nothing mattered but your will to succeed, not your color, not your ethnic background, not your education, not your social status.

696
00:53:47,232 --> 00:53:53,428
If you want to change the world, measure a person by the size of their heart, not by the size of their flippers.

697
00:53:55,232 --> 00:54:02,132
Several times a week, the instructors would line up the class and do a uniform inspection. It was exceptionally thorough.

698
00:54:02,932 --> 00:54:09,532
Your hat had to be perfectly starched, your uniform immaculate. pressed, your belt buckle shiny and void of any smudges.

699
00:54:10,732 --> 00:54:13,792
But it seemed that no matter how much effort you put into

700
00:54:13,792 --> 00:54:15,832
starching your hat or pressing your uniform or

701
00:54:15,832 --> 00:54:18,127
polishing your belt buckle, it just wasn't good enough.

702
00:54:18,932 --> 00:54:20,932
The instructors would find something wrong.

703
00:54:21,832 --> 00:54:24,732
For failing uniform inspection, the student had to run

704
00:54:25,532 --> 00:54:27,872
fully clothed into the surf zone, then wet

705
00:54:27,872 --> 00:54:30,212
from head to toe, roll around on the

706
00:54:30,212 --> 00:54:33,430
beach until every part of your body was covered with sand.

707
00:54:34,232 --> 00:54:36,632
The effect was known as a sugar cookie.

708
00:54:38,772 --> 00:54:42,372
You stayed in the uniform the rest of the day, cold, wet, and sandy.

709
00:54:43,472 --> 00:54:46,599
There were many a student who just couldn't accept the fact that

710
00:54:46,599 --> 00:54:48,683
all their efforts were in vain, that no

711
00:54:48,683 --> 00:54:52,070
matter how hard they tried to get the uniform right, it went unappreciated.

712
00:54:52,772 --> 00:54:55,172
Those students didn't make it through training.

713
00:54:55,172 --> 00:54:58,572
Those students didn't understand the purpose of the drill.

714
00:54:59,372 --> 00:55:00,898
You were never going to succeed.

715
00:55:00,898 --> 00:55:04,968
You were never going to have a perfect uniform. The instructors weren't going to allow it.

716
00:55:06,072 --> 00:55:12,172
Sometimes, no matter how well you prepare or how well you perform, you still end up as a sugar cookie.

717
00:55:13,072 --> 00:55:14,872
It's just the way life is sometimes.

718
00:55:15,772 --> 00:55:20,572
If you want to change the world, get over being a sugar cookie and keep moving forward.

719
00:55:22,072 --> 00:55:24,629
Every day during training, you were challenged

720
00:55:24,629 --> 00:55:27,186
with multiple physical events, long runs, long

721
00:55:27,186 --> 00:55:29,378
swims, obstacle courses, hours of calisthenics,

722
00:55:29,378 --> 00:55:31,570
something designed to test your mettle.

723
00:55:32,072 --> 00:55:34,672
Every event had standards, times you had to meet.

724
00:55:34,672 --> 00:55:39,472
If you failed to meet those times, those standards, your name was posted on a list.

725
00:55:40,072 --> 00:55:45,272
And at the end of the day, those on the list were invited to a circus.

726
00:55:45,872 --> 00:55:51,168
A circus was two hours of additional calisthenics designed to wear you down, to break your spirit, to force you to quit.

727
00:55:51,772 --> 00:55:53,672
No one wanted a circus.

728
00:55:54,372 --> 00:55:57,272
A circus meant that for that day, you didn't measure up.

729
00:55:57,772 --> 00:56:03,272
A circus meant more fatigue, and more fatigue meant that the following day would be more difficult, and more circuses were likely.

730
00:56:04,472 --> 00:56:10,572
But at some time during SEAL training, everyone, Everyone made the circus list.

731
00:56:11,872 --> 00:56:16,272
But an interesting thing happened to those who were constantly on the list.

732
00:56:17,172 --> 00:56:23,672
Over time, those students who did two hours of extra calisthenics got stronger and stronger.

733
00:56:24,572 --> 00:56:27,572
The pain of the circuses built inner strength and physical resiliency.

734
00:56:29,272 --> 00:56:30,672
Life is filled with circuses.

735
00:56:31,772 --> 00:56:34,672
You will fail. You will likely fail often.

736
00:56:34,872 --> 00:56:35,772
It will be painful.

737
00:56:36,472 --> 00:56:37,672
It will be discouraging.

738
00:56:38,072 --> 00:56:40,772
At times, it will test you to your very core.

739
00:56:41,772 --> 00:56:45,872
But if you want to change the world, don't be afraid of the circuses.

740
00:56:47,372 --> 00:56:50,472
At least twice a week, the trainees were required to run the obstacle course.

741
00:56:51,872 --> 00:56:58,046
The obstacle course contained 25 obstacles, including a 10-foot wall, a 30-foot cargo net, a barbed wire crawl, to name a few.

742
00:56:58,972 --> 00:57:02,072
But the most challenging obstacle was the slide for life.

743
00:57:02,772 --> 00:57:10,072
It had a three-level, 30-foot tower at one end and a one-level tower at the other. In between was a 200-foot-long rope.

744
00:57:10,872 --> 00:57:13,099
You had to climb the three-tiered tower,

745
00:57:13,099 --> 00:57:15,326
and once at the top, you grabbed

746
00:57:15,326 --> 00:57:17,235
the rope, swung underneath the rope,

747
00:57:17,235 --> 00:57:21,371
and pulled yourself hand over hand until you got to the other end.

748
00:57:21,872 --> 00:57:26,372
The record for the obstacle course had stood for years when my class began in 1977.

749
00:57:26,872 --> 00:57:28,072
The record seemed unbeatable.

750
00:57:28,972 --> 00:57:34,372
Until one day a student decided to go down the slide for life head first.

751
00:57:35,272 --> 00:57:42,272
Instead of swinging his body underneath the rope, and inching his way down, he bravely mounted the top of the rope and thrust himself forward.

752
00:57:42,572 --> 00:57:46,772
It was a dangerous move, seemingly foolish and fraught with risk.

753
00:57:47,272 --> 00:57:49,272
Failure could mean injury and being dropped from the course.

754
00:57:49,272 --> 00:57:53,372
Without hesitation, the student slid down the rope perilously fast.

755
00:57:53,972 --> 00:57:57,172
Instead of several minutes, it only took him half that time.

756
00:57:57,872 --> 00:58:01,072
And by the end of the course, he had broken the record.

757
00:58:02,372 --> 00:58:06,872
If you want to change the world, sometimes you have to slide down the obstacles head first.

758
00:58:08,872 --> 00:58:14,470
During the land warfare phase of training, the students are flown out to San Clemente Island, which lies off the coast of San Diego.

759
00:58:15,472 --> 00:58:18,572
The waters off San Clemente are a breeding ground for the great white sharks.

760
00:58:19,572 --> 00:58:22,772
To pass SEAL training, there are a series of long swims that must be completed.

761
00:58:23,472 --> 00:58:24,572
One is the night swim.

762
00:58:25,372 --> 00:58:28,072
Before the swim, the instructors joyfully brief the students.

763
00:58:28,972 --> 00:58:33,572
On all the species of sharks that inhabit the waters off San Clemente.

764
00:58:34,672 --> 00:58:42,367
They assure you, however, that no student has ever been eaten by a shark, at least not that they can remember.

765
00:58:44,072 --> 00:58:49,972
But you are also taught that if a shark begins to circle your position, Stand your ground.

766
00:58:50,772 --> 00:58:51,872
Do not swim away.

767
00:58:52,772 --> 00:58:53,972
Do not act afraid.

768
00:58:54,972 --> 00:58:58,688
And if a shark, hungry for a midnight snack, darts towards you,

769
00:58:58,688 --> 00:59:01,165
then summons up all your strength and punch

770
00:59:01,165 --> 00:59:04,571
him in the snout, and he will turn and swim away.

771
00:59:06,072 --> 00:59:07,072
There are a lot of sharks in the world.

772
00:59:08,472 --> 00:59:11,972
If you hope to complete the swim, you will have to deal with them.

773
00:59:13,072 --> 00:59:14,472
So if you want to change the world,

774
00:59:16,072 --> 00:59:17,372
Don't back down from the sharks.

775
00:59:19,172 --> 00:59:23,172
As Navy SEALs, one of our jobs is to conduct underwater attacks against enemy shipping.

776
00:59:24,072 --> 00:59:26,872
We practice this technique extensively during training.

777
00:59:27,772 --> 00:59:31,252
The ship attack mission is where a pair of SEAL divers is

778
00:59:31,252 --> 00:59:33,572
dropped off outside an enemy harbor and then

779
00:59:33,572 --> 00:59:39,372
swims well over two miles underwater using nothing but a depth gauge and a compass to get to the target.

780
00:59:40,572 --> 00:59:47,372
During the entire swim, even well below the surface, there is some light that comes through.

781
00:59:48,272 --> 00:59:51,272
It is comforting to know that there is open water above you.

782
00:59:52,772 --> 00:59:55,076
But as you approach the ship, which is

783
00:59:55,076 --> 00:59:57,092
tied to appear, the light begins to

784
00:59:57,092 --> 00:59:59,972
fade. The steel structure of the ship blocks the moonlight.

785
01:00:00,572 --> 01:00:02,672
It blocks the surrounding street lamps.

786
01:00:03,472 --> 01:00:05,772
It blocks all ambient light.

787
01:00:06,672 --> 01:00:14,069
To be successful in your mission, you have to swim under the ship and find the keel, the center line, and the deepest part of the ship. This is your objective.

788
01:00:14,972 --> 01:00:20,203
But the keel is also the darkest part of the ship, where you cannot see your hand in

789
01:00:20,203 --> 01:00:22,237
front of your face, where the noise

790
01:00:22,237 --> 01:00:27,469
from the ship's machinery is deafening, and where it gets to be easily disoriented, and you can fail.

791
01:00:27,972 --> 01:00:33,072
Every SEAL knows that under the keel, at that darkest moment of the mission,

792
01:00:33,872 --> 01:00:36,472
is a time when you need to be calm.

793
01:00:37,372 --> 01:00:39,416
when you must be calm, when

794
01:00:39,416 --> 01:00:42,141
you must be composed, when all your tactical

795
01:00:42,141 --> 01:00:46,570
skills, your physical power, and your inner strength must be brought to bear.

796
01:00:47,872 --> 01:00:53,272
If you want to change the world, you must be your very best in the darkest moments.

797
01:00:54,972 --> 01:00:57,272
The ninth week of training is referred to as Hell Week.

798
01:00:58,272 --> 01:01:05,872
It is six days of no sleep, constant physical and mental harassment, and one special day at the mudflats.

799
01:01:06,272 --> 01:01:09,272
The mudflats are an area between San Diego and Tijuana

800
01:01:09,272 --> 01:01:11,672
where the water runs off and creates the

801
01:01:11,672 --> 01:01:15,572
Tijuana sloughs, a swampy patch of terrain where the mud will engulf you.

802
01:01:16,672 --> 01:01:20,145
It is on Wednesday of Hell Week that you paddle down to

803
01:01:20,145 --> 01:01:22,171
the mudflats and spend the next 15 hours

804
01:01:22,171 --> 01:01:27,381
trying to survive this freezing cold, the howling wind, and the incessant pressure to quit from the instructors.

805
01:01:29,072 --> 01:01:35,872
As the sun began to set that Wednesday evening, my training class, having committed some egregious infraction of the rules,

806
01:01:36,872 --> 01:01:37,972
was ordered into the mud.

807
01:01:38,972 --> 01:01:43,072
The mud consumed each man until there was nothing visible but our heads.

808
01:01:44,172 --> 01:01:48,172
The instructors told us we could leave the mud if only five men would quit.

809
01:01:48,972 --> 01:01:52,872
Only five men, just five men, and we could get out of the oppressive cold.

810
01:01:54,172 --> 01:01:57,072
Looking around the mud flat, it was apparent that some students were about to give up.

811
01:01:58,472 --> 01:02:01,620
It was still over eight hours until the sun came

812
01:02:01,620 --> 01:02:06,971
up, eight more hours of bone-chilling cold, the chattering teeth and the shivering moans of the trainees.

813
01:02:07,072 --> 01:02:10,072
These were so loud, it was hard to hear anything.

814
01:02:11,172 --> 01:02:14,272
And then one voice began to echo through the night.

815
01:02:15,872 --> 01:02:17,372
One voice raised in song.

816
01:02:18,872 --> 01:02:23,472
The song was terribly out of tune, but sung with great enthusiasm.

817
01:02:24,472 --> 01:02:29,472
One voice became two, and two became three, and before long, everyone in the class was singing.

818
01:02:30,172 --> 01:02:34,972
The instructors threatened us with more time in the mud if we kept up the singing, but the singing persisted.

819
01:02:35,672 --> 01:02:42,469
And somehow the mud seemed a little warmer, and the wind a little tamer, and the dawn not so far away.

820
01:02:43,472 --> 01:02:48,872
If I have learned anything in my time traveling the world, it is the power of hope.

821
01:02:49,472 --> 01:02:56,772
The power of one person, a Washington, a Lincoln, King, Mandela, and even a young girl from Pakistan, Malala.

822
01:02:57,172 --> 01:03:00,972
One person can change the world by giving people hope.

823
01:03:01,372 --> 01:03:06,072
So if you want to change the world, start singing when you're up to your neck in mud.

824
01:03:07,972 --> 01:03:15,172
Finally, in SEAL training, there's a bell, a brass bell that hangs in the center of the compound for all the students to see.

825
01:03:16,072 --> 01:03:20,072
All you have to do to quit is ring the bell.

826
01:03:21,072 --> 01:03:24,272
Ring the bell, and you no longer have to wake up at 5 o'clock.

827
01:03:24,372 --> 01:03:28,572
Ring the bell, and you no longer have to be in the freezing cold swims.

828
01:03:29,072 --> 01:03:36,267
Ring the bell, and you no longer have to do the runs, the obstacle course, the PT, and you no longer have to endure the hardship.

829
01:03:39,172 --> 01:03:40,972
All you have to do is ring the bell to get out.

830
01:03:42,872 --> 01:03:48,172
If you want to change the world, don't ever, ever ring the bell.

831
01:03:49,772 --> 01:03:52,035
To the class of 2014, you are moments

832
01:03:52,035 --> 01:03:54,621
away from graduating, moments away from beginning your

833
01:03:54,621 --> 01:03:59,147
journey through life, moments away from starting to change the world for the better.

834
01:04:00,272 --> 01:04:01,572
It will not be easy.

835
01:04:02,172 --> 01:04:07,272
But you are the class of 2014, the class that can affect the lives of 800 million people in the next century.

836
01:04:07,972 --> 01:04:09,872
Start each day with a task completed.

837
01:04:10,572 --> 01:04:12,172
Find someone to help you through life.

838
01:04:12,272 --> 01:04:13,672
Respect everyone.

839
01:04:14,272 --> 01:04:16,672
Know that life is not fair and that you will fail often.

840
01:04:17,372 --> 01:04:24,967
But if you take some risks, step up when the times are the toughest, face down the bullies, lift up the downtrodden, and never, ever give up.

841
01:04:25,372 --> 01:04:33,368
If you do these things, the next generation and the generations that follow will live in a world far better than the one we have today.

842
01:04:33,872 --> 01:04:38,872
And what started here will indeed have changed the world for the better.

843
01:04:39,772 --> 01:04:40,672
Thank you very much.

844
01:04:41,072 --> 01:04:41,672
Hook them horns.

845
01:04:44,424 --> 01:04:45,924
I really hope you enjoyed that video.

846
01:04:46,524 --> 01:04:50,324
It's so important that you can relate trading to something that's important to you.

847
01:04:51,024 --> 01:04:53,617
I'd like to go over a few of the key

848
01:04:53,617 --> 01:04:55,692
takeaways from that video and we can see

849
01:04:55,692 --> 01:04:59,323
how the Navy, we can relate trading to the Navy in so many ways.

850
01:04:59,924 --> 01:05:06,924
Personally, I like golf a lot and I found that you can relate golf to trading almost perfectly.

851
01:05:07,524 --> 01:05:10,524
But anyways, let's go through this video and see what some of the key takeaways were.

852
01:05:11,024 --> 01:05:13,424
Firstly, discipline every day.

853
01:05:14,324 --> 01:05:20,524
The general talks about starting by making your bed. Pay attention to the small things and accomplish them perfectly.

854
01:05:21,024 --> 01:05:27,723
So every morning when you get up, get up at the same time. Start with the same routine. Have discipline the minute you open your eyes.

855
01:05:28,024 --> 01:05:32,324
If you do that, it will become a habit not just in your daily lives, but in your trading.

856
01:05:33,424 --> 01:05:39,524
Don't do it alone. Find those families, those friends, the community, the colleagues. That's what we are for, mentors.

857
01:05:39,824 --> 01:05:46,120
That's what the Axia membership is all about, is being in a community of like-minded people going through similar things as you.

858
01:05:46,824 --> 01:05:53,920
If you can find these kind of people, hold on to them, don't let go of them, because this is going to be tough, you're going to need all the help you can get.

859
01:05:55,624 --> 01:05:56,324
Fair for all.

860
01:05:57,524 --> 01:06:04,624
Markets don't reward age, race, culture, intelligence, beauty, height, but they reward the size of your heart.

861
01:06:05,324 --> 01:06:06,724
That's an important thing to understand.

862
01:06:07,124 --> 01:06:09,852
You don't have to be smart to be a trader. You don't have to

863
01:06:09,852 --> 01:06:14,722
be a straight A student. What you do have to do is have one hell of a passion and a love for what you're doing.

864
01:06:15,224 --> 01:06:18,324
If you have that, it's a vital ingredient to success in trading.

865
01:06:19,824 --> 01:06:22,324
How well you prepare determines how well you succeed.

866
01:06:22,924 --> 01:06:28,924
So crucial. I see so many guys coming in Monday morning, they haven't even prepared their thoughts over the weekend.

867
01:06:29,024 --> 01:06:31,324
They haven't even thought about what happened in the past week.

868
01:06:31,624 --> 01:06:34,990
